    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (77.36), who represent our primary offensive threats against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a weak SP_xERA of 4.35, making him the highest-projected asset in our 5x5 build. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** (71.57) are poised for high-output days against Bubba Chandler; the matchup provides an excellent SP_xERA environment (4.85) that helps offset the volatility typically associated with their mid-order slots. We are heavily leaning into the stolen base potential here, as **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Andy Pages** all face starters with slow delivery profiles, providing a high-ceiling opportunity to gain ground in our scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Dominic Smith** (38.13) from the utility slot. While he carried a decent base projection, his performance metrics against Misiorowski fell below our mandatory 40.0 efficiency floor, leading us to favor the raw upside of **Coby Mayo** (56.02). **Coby Mayo** earns the nod primarily due to the significant park factors in his favor and the chance for high-leverage counting stats, even against a tough arm like Peralta. We are monitoring two specific weather risks: **Miguel Vargas** and **Luis Robert Jr.** are both impacted by a 37% rain risk. While both are currently in the starting lineup, their output could be truncated, and we remain wary of any potential delays impacting their rhythm. We continue to manage our remaining depth\u2014including **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White**\u2014while keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sidelined due to injury or availability concerns.",
